#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Concepts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clubs, users and roles {#clubs-users-and-roles}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **club** is a tenant: everything in Standblatt belongs to exactly one club, and clubs never see each other's data. The platform operator creates clubs and user accounts in the [admin panel](../admin-guide/admin-panel.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:8
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Users** are personal accounts. One account can belong to several clubs, with one role per club:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Role | Can |\n|---|---|\n| **Admin** | everything: ranges, events, programmes, kiosk links, users of the club, special prizes, closing events |\n| **Staff** | run events: register shooters, enter results, print, reservations; read everything else |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranges and lanes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **range** (German *Stand*) is a shooting range of the club with a number of **lanes** (*Scheiben*). Lanes can be marked out of service. Printers and the print agent belong to a range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Events and programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "An **event** (*Anlass*) is a competition on one or more ranges on one or more days (the date is the main day; further days cover pre-shooting and multi-day events). It has a language, which is used for printed documents and kiosk screens, and a few settings such as the club excluded from the club competition."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "An event offers **programmes** (*Stiche*): each programme has **series** (*Passen*) with a number of shots and maximum points, **prices** per age category and **award tiers** (wreath cards or prizes in kind) with a minimum total per age category. Programmes with the same name are **variants** (for example *Sport* and *Supported*); a shooter shoots one variant. A programme can be **combinable** with another programme: it then takes some of its series from that programme instead of being shot separately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooters, registrations and entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Shooters** are the people who shoot. Each club keeps its own shooter master data, together with the **clubs** shooters belong to (the shooter's own club, not to be confused with the tenant club).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **registration** puts a shooter on the event, optionally on a lane, with one or more programmes. Each programme of a registration is an **entry**. A registration is *registered* (waiting), *shooting* (on a lane) or *completed* (all programmes have results; the lane is free again)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Results, awards and rankings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Results** are the points per series, optionally with mouches (inner tens). Once all series are in, the shooter may receive one of the **awards** the total reaches in the shooter's age category. **Rankings** order all results of a programme by the [SSV rules](../reference/rules.md#ranking).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Age categories {#age-categories}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "The age category follows from the birth year and the year of the event:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:50
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Category | Short | Age in the event year |\n|---|---|---|\n| U10 | U10 | up to 9 |\n| U13 | U13 | 10–12 |\n| U15 | U15 | 13–14 |\n| U17 | U17 | 15–16 |\n| U19 | U19 | 17–18 |\n| U21 | U21 | 19–20 |\n| Elite | E | 21–45 |\n| Senior | S | 46–59 |\n| Veteran | V | 60–69 |\n| Senior veteran | SV | 70 and older |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "A shooter without a birthday counts as Elite."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/concepts.md:67
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| English (Standblatt) | German | French | Italian |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Range | Stand | Stand | Stand |\n| Lane | Scheibe | Cible | Bersaglio |\n| Event | Anlass | Manifestation | Manifestazione |\n| Programme | Stich / Programm | Programme | Programma |\n| Series | Passe | Passe | Serie |\n| Award | Auszeichnung | Distinction | Distinzione |\n| Wreath card | Kranzkarte | Carte-couronne | Carta corona |\n| Prize in kind | Naturalgabe | Prix en nature | Premio in natura |\n| Club competition | Vereinskonkurrenz | Concours de sections | Concorso di sezione |\n| Lane sheet | Standblatt | Feuille de stand | Foglio di stand |\n| Control strip | Kontrollstreifen | Bande de contrôle | Striscia di controllo |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Your first event"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "This walk-through takes a club from an empty account to a running competition. It assumes the platform operator has created the club and your account as its admin (see [Admin panel](../admin-guide/admin-panel.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "1. Log in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the app, log in with the account you were given and pick your language in the user menu at the bottom of the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "As long as the club has no event, the **Events** page shows a **Getting started** checklist with the steps below; each open step has a button that takes you there. An event without active programmes shows the same checklist instead of its dashboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:12
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Login](../images/screenshots/login.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "2. Set up the range"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Ranges**, create the range with its number of lanes and mark lanes that are out of service. If you print at the range, add a print agent later (see [Printing](../user-guide/printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3. Load the shooters"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Shooters**, import your shooter list as a CSV file (see [CSV import](../reference/csv-import.md)) or create shooters one by one. Shooters can also be created at the desk during the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "4. Create the event"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Events**, create the event: name, date, range, organizer and the language of documents and kiosk screens. If you held the event last year, open last year's event and use **Copy for next year** instead: it takes over the settings and all programmes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The events of a club](../images/screenshots/events.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5. Add the programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "In the event's **Setup**, add the programmes: from the editor, from the programme library, from a programme file or by copying them from an earlier event. Check prices, award tiers, variants and combinations, and set up [special prizes](../user-guide/programmes.md#special-prizes) if your event awards them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Event setup](../images/screenshots/setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "6. Kiosk screens and printers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Still in Setup, on the *Kiosk displays* tab, create a kiosk link for each screen in the hall (see [Rankings and kiosk](../user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md)). Under Ranges → Printing, assign a printer to each document (see [Printing](../user-guide/printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "7. Run the event"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "On the **Dashboard**, press ++f4++, search the shooter, register them on a lane and let the lane sheet print. Enter the results when the shooter hands in the targets; the rankings and kiosk screens update immediately. See [Dashboard](../user-guide/dashboard.md), [Registrations](../user-guide/registrations.md) and [Results](../user-guide/results.md)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "8. After the event"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/getting-started/first-event.md:43
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Statistics**, download the reports (financial report, awards, club competition, special prizes …). When everything is settled, **close** the event in Setup (*Copy & close* tab): the rankings are released to the shooters' personal training logs, and the event stays readable but can no longer be changed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Standblatt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt runs shooting competitions at the range: registration, lane assignment, result entry, awards, live rankings and the paperwork afterwards. It follows the rules of the Swiss Shooting Sport Federation (SSV/FST) and is used by clubs for events like an air pistol championship."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "With [My training](my-training/index.md) every shooter also gets a personal shooting diary on the phone: log a session in seconds, see the trend, the best series and where the group sits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The event dashboard](images/screenshots/dashboard.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Registration at the desk**: find a shooter by name, license number or a scanned code, pick a lane and the programmes, print the lane sheet and the control strip."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Results**: enter the series, the totals and awards follow the programme's rules; combined programmes take their series from another programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Live rankings**: ranked by the SSV rules, on the staff pages and on kiosk screens in the hall, updated the moment a result is saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Documents**: lane sheets, control strips, result sheets, wreath cards and rankings as PDF, printed at the range through a small print agent."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Reports**: statistics, club competition, revenue, awards, special prizes, all as PDF and CSV."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**My training**: a personal training log with fast capture, hits on the target, progress and goals; competition results from Standblatt events are added with one tap."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/index.md:18
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Every club for itself**: each club keeps its own shooters, ranges, events and users. The interface is available in English, German, French and Italian."
msgstr ""

