#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every Standblatt user has My training: club users open it from the start page or the user menu, shooters without a club sign up themselves. Email address, password, language, second factor and deleting the account live on the [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account) page, which **Account** in the sidebar or **Settings → Account** opens."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Sign up"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open **Create an account** on the login page. You need your name, your email address and a password of at least 10 characters. You are logged in right away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Sign-up](../images/screenshots/my-signup.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt sends you a link to confirm your email address. Until you confirm it, a note on the Today page reminds you; **Send again** sends a new link. The link is valid for seven days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Forgot your password? Use **Forgot your password?** on the login page. You get a link that is valid for one hour. Setting a new password logs you out everywhere. Logged in, you change the password under [Account](../user-guide/login-language.md#account)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Accounts created by a club admin log in with their user name instead of an email; they can add an email address under **Settings → Email**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Profile and competition results {#competitions}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "Under **Settings → Profile** you can enter your **birthday** and **license number**. With both, Standblatt finds your results from events run with Standblatt by any club, for example the club championship. They show up in the **Log** under *Your competition results* once the club has closed the event, that is, once the ranking is final. Each result carries your **rank** in the programme (for example *Rank 12 of 87*). Choose the discipline and tap **Add**, or **Add all**. Added results become competition sessions with their series and keep the rank."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Own disciplines"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "Six disciplines are built in: air pistol and air rifle 10 m, pistol 25 m and 50 m, rifle 50 m and 300 m. For anything else, e.g. a field programme, add **Own discipline** in the settings with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "the usual number of series and shots per series,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "whole or decimal (up to 10.9) scoring and the highest value of a shot,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "optionally a target face for tapping hits."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Weapons {#weapons}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shoot more than one gun, e.g. two air pistols? Add them under **Settings → Weapons** with a name of your choice; the calibre does not matter. Choose the weapon when you save a session and [Progress](progress.md#weapons-compared) compares them. Renaming a weapon keeps its sessions. Deleting it keeps the sessions too, they just have no weapon any more."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "API tokens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Want to import sessions from another app or analyse your log with your own script? Create a token under **Settings → API tokens**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "a **name** that tells you later what uses it,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "the **permissions**: *Read sessions* and/or *Log and change sessions*,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "when it **expires**: in 30 or 90 days, in a year, or never."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "The token (`sb_…`) is shown only once; copy it right away. Scripts send it as `Authorization: Bearer sb_…` (or `X-API-Key: sb_…`). It works for your sessions, disciplines, weapons, goals, statistics and the export, but never for your password, email, account or other tokens, and never for club data. The list shows when each token was last used; revoking one stops it at once. See the [API reference](../developer/api.md) for the endpoints."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Install the app"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt is a web app that can be installed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Android / Chrome**: Settings → **Install**, or *Add to home screen* in the browser menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:49
#, markdown-text
msgid "**iPhone**: Share → *Add to Home Screen*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:51
#, markdown-text
msgid "Installed, it starts full screen. A long press on the icon offers *Start training*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:52
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Your data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Export all sessions (CSV)** downloads every series of every session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/account.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Delete account** removes the account with all sessions, goals and settings after you enter your password. Accounts that belong to a club must first be removed from the club by its admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "My training"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "My training is a personal shooting diary. Every shooter can use it, whether or not their club runs events with Standblatt. It answers one question: **does my training work?**"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"grid\" markdown>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Today on a phone](../images/screenshots/my-today.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress of a discipline](../images/screenshots/my-progress.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Logging takes seconds.** After a session you tap the + button, type the series totals on the number pad and save. Standblatt moves on to the next series by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**As detailed as you like.** Log only the series totals, every shot value, or tap every hit on the target. You can switch per series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Feedback right away.** After saving you see how the session ranks among your sessions of the same length and how it compares with your last 30 days."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Progress you can read.** Trend, personal best, goal, series curve, shot values, the size and centre of your group, what your tags tell you and how your weapons compare."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Competitions come for free.** Results from events run with Standblatt are found by your license number and birthday once the club closes the event, and added with one tap, rank included."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Works at the range.** Install it on the home screen. Without signal, sessions are kept on the phone and uploaded later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Your data stays yours.** Export everything as CSV at any time and delete your account whenever you want."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Page | What it is for |\n|---|---|\n| **Today** | start a session, this week's activity, your recent trend and sessions |\n| **Log** | every session, filtered by discipline and kind, competition results waiting to be added |\n| **Progress** | the analysis of one discipline, see [Progress explained](progress.md) |\n| **Settings** | profile (name, birthday and license number for the competition match), own disciplines, weapons, app, API tokens, export; **Account** for email, password, language, second factor and deleting the account |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a phone the pages are in the bar at the bottom, with the + button in the middle. On a larger screen they are in the sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Access and price"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "My training is free for every user of the server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/index.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Club staff accounts can use My training too: open **My training** in the user menu of the club sidebar."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging a session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap the **+** button, or a discipline under **Start training** on the Today page. The session opens full screen with your last discipline already selected."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Series totals on the number pad](../images/screenshots/my-train-series.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "At the top you see the running total, the number of shots and the average per shot. Below that is a chip for every series. Tap a chip to correct that series, tap **+** to add one, or use **Remove series** for the current one. The minus and plus next to \"10 shots\" change the number of shots of the current series, e.g. for a 5-shot series at 25 m."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Three ways to enter a series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Choose the input for the current series at the top right. You can mix them in one session, e.g. totals for the first four series and every shot for the last two."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Series**\n: Type the series total. As soon as no further digit could make the number valid, Standblatt takes it and jumps to the next series. \"9\", \"3\" gives 93 and moves on; a 100 needs \"1\", \"0\", \"0\". With decimal scoring the point is added for you: \"1\", \"0\", \"2\", \"7\" gives 102.7. **Next** takes the number as it is.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Shots**\n: Tap the value of every shot. With decimal scoring type two digits, e.g. \"9\", \"7\" for 9.7, or three for a ten, e.g. \"1\", \"0\", \"4\" for 10.4. After the last shot of a series the next series starts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Target**\n: Tap where every shot hit. Standblatt computes the value from the target face of the discipline, with decimals if the discipline is scored that way. The magnifier switches between the black and the whole target. This is the only way to get the [group analysis](progress.md#group).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:23
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Tapping hits on the target](../images/screenshots/my-train-target.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "On a computer you can type the digits, **Backspace** and **Enter** on the keyboard."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Save"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the last series is complete, or when you tap **Finish**, the save sheet opens. Everything in it is optional:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Training or competition**: competitions appear as their own dots in the trend and are compared with your training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Weapon**: which of your [weapons](account.md#weapons) you shot with. A new session starts with the weapon of your last session in the same discipline; tap it again to clear it, or add a new weapon right there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**How did it feel?**: five faces from bad to great."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Tags**: short words for what was special, e.g. *new grip*, *tired*, *new pellets*. Progress compares the sessions with a tag to your average."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "**When**, **where**, **notes**. *Where* starts with the place of your last training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![After saving](../images/screenshots/my-result.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid "After saving Standblatt tells you right away:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "whether the session is a **new personal best**, or which place it takes among your sessions with the same number of shots;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "how many points per shot it is above or below the average of the **30 days before**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:43
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Unfinished sessions and offline"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:46
#, markdown-text
msgid "The session is kept on the device while you type. If you close the browser or the phone locks, it comes back the next time you start a session."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "If there is no connection when you save, the session is kept on the device and uploaded as soon as you are online again. A note on the Today page shows how many sessions are waiting. A retried upload never creates a session twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "Waiting sessions belong to the account that typed them. If your login expired in the meantime, log in again and they are uploaded; another person logging in on the same device does not get them. If the server refuses one, for example because its discipline was deleted, a note shows the reason and you can **Discard** it. Only new sessions can be saved offline; changing a session needs a connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:52
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once you opened the app online, it also opens without a connection and shows your last data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:53
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Changing or deleting a session"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/logging.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the session in the **Log** and use the pencil to change it, or the bin to delete it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Progress explained"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Progress** analyses all sessions of one discipline; choose it at the top right. Everything is computed from the sessions in your log, nothing is estimated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Progress](../images/screenshots/my-progress.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Points per shot"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Sessions differ in length: a 50-shot match, two series after work, a 40-shot competition. Standblatt compares them by **points per shot**, the total divided by the number of shots. 9.30 per shot is 465 over 50 shots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:11
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Key figures"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Last 30 days**\n: points per shot over all sessions of the last 30 days. The arrow shows the change against the 30 days before.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Personal best**\n: the highest total among sessions with the standard number of shots of the discipline, e.g. 60 for air pistol. Tap it to open the session.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Sessions**\n: number of sessions and shots logged in this discipline.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Competition vs. training**\n: points per shot in competitions minus points per shot in training. A negative number means you lose points under pressure.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Trend"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every session is a dot, competitions in amber. The line is the moving average of the last five sessions, so a single bad day does not hide the direction. A dashed line shows your goal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Goal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Set the total you want to reach over the standard number of shots, optionally with a date. The bar compares it with your last 30 days and tells you how much is missing per shot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Series curve"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "Points per shot of the first, second, third … series over all sessions. It shows whether you need a series to warm up, or lose concentration towards the end. The strongest series is highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shot values"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "How often each value occurred, from the sessions where you logged every shot or tapped the hits. Decimal values count towards their whole number, so 9.7 counts as a 9."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:41
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Group {#group}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "From the hits you tapped on the target in your last ten sessions with hits:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Group size** is twice the average distance of your hits from their centre, in mm. It is a robust measure of how tight you shoot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Off centre** is the distance of that centre from the middle of the target."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the centre sits clearly to one side, Standblatt tells you which way to adjust the sight. Check your hold and trigger first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:50
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Group on the target](../images/screenshots/my-session.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:51
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Weapons compared {#weapons-compared}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:54
#, markdown-text
msgid "As soon as sessions of a discipline were shot with at least two of your weapons, a table compares them: the points per shot of all their sessions, of the last 30 days and the best total over the full match. The weapon with the highest average is on top. Sessions without a weapon are not part of it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:56
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Two air pistols compared](../images/screenshots/my-weapons.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:58
#, markdown-text
msgid "Tap a weapon, or choose it in the weapon list at the top, and every figure on the page (key figures, trend, series curve, shot values and group) only counts the sessions shot with it. *All weapons* shows everything again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:59
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What your tags tell you"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/my-training/progress.md:61
#, markdown-text
msgid "For every tag used on at least two sessions: the points per shot of those sessions and the difference to your overall average. Sorted from the best to the worst, this is where you find out whether the new grip pays off."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Codes and barcodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration code (QR)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Lane sheets and control strips carry a QR code with"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "REGCODEAAAA<registration>AAAAL<license or 0>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "for example `REGCODEAAAA42AAAAL100109`. A hand scanner types it into the search field of the dashboard and presses Enter; Standblatt opens the results of that registration. The license part guards against a code from another shooter; a code of another event is refused."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:13
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programme barcode (Interleaved 2 of 5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/codes.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme can have a barcode, printed as Interleaved 2 of 5 next to the programme on the lane sheet (only the digits count, padded to an even number of digits). Electronic scoring systems use it to pick the programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "CSV import"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Club admins import shooters on the **Shooters** page. The file needs a header row; the separator (`;` or `,`) is taken from it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (text)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "license;firstname;lastname;birthday;postalcode;city;club\n100100;Sandra;Example;1969-06-02;9050;Appenzell;PS Example\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Column | Required | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `firstname` | yes | |\n| `lastname` | yes | |\n| `license` | no | also `licensenumber`; purely numeric numbers are padded to six digits |\n| `birthday` | no | `YYYY-MM-DD` or `DD.MM.YYYY` |\n| `postalcode`, `city` | no | |\n| `club` | no | the shooter's club; missing clubs are created |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "One line per shooter and club; a shooter in two clubs appears twice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooters are matched by license number, or by name and birthday when there is none. Existing shooters are updated, nothing is deleted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/csv-import.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A file with invalid lines is rejected as a whole, with the list of lines to fix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programme file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Export** in the programme menu downloads a programme as `<name>.programme.json`; **Programme file** under *Add from …* imports it into another event or another club. The platform operator uploads the same files to the global programme library.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (json)
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\n  \"format\": \"standblatt.programme\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"programme\": {\n    \"name\": \"Championship\",\n    \"variant\": \"Sport\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"barcode\": \"700005002334864165956154\",\n    \"countsForClubCompetition\": true,\n    \"showOnRankings\": true,\n    \"series\": [\n      { \"shots\": 10, \"maxPoints\": 100, \"trackMouches\": false, \"name\": \"\" }\n    ],\n    \"prices\": [\n      { \"ageCategory\": \"elite\", \"price\": 20 }\n    ],\n    \"awards\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Wreath card CHF 10\",\n        \"kind\": \"card\",\n        \"value\": 10,\n        \"limits\": [{ \"ageCategory\": \"elite\", \"points\": 370 }]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`ageCategory` is one of `u10`, `u13`, `u15`, `u17`, `u19`, `u21`, `elite`, `senior`, `veteran`, `senior_veteran`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`kind` is `card` (wreath card, printed) or `natural` (prize in kind)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "`showOnRankings` is the *Show on kiosk displays* switch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/programme-file.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "Combinations and special prizes are settings of the programme within an event and are not part of the file; copying programmes from an earlier event keeps them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Competition rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "This page describes the rules exactly as Standblatt implements them. They live in `internal/domain` and are covered by unit tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Age category"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "The category follows from *event year − birth year*; see the table in [Concepts](../getting-started/concepts.md#age-categories). Without a birthday a shooter counts as Elite. The category is fixed when the shooter registers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:9
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "A registration is refused when:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme does not belong to the event, is chosen twice or is not active;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme has no price for the shooter's age category (\"not open to the age category\");"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "two variants of the same programme are chosen;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "a programme takes series from another programme that is not chosen, or the number of picked series does not match;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "the lane is taken by another active registration or is out of service;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "the shooter is already registered for one of the programmes at this event (a shooter shoots each programme once per event; another variant in a separate registration is fine)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A reserved lane can still be used after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:22 ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Results"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every series must be entered. Points lie between 0 and the series maximum (by default shots × 10), mouches between 0 and the number of shots, and only on series that track mouches. Saving results gives the most valuable award the total reaches; saving them again keeps the chosen award as long as the new total still reaches it, otherwise the most valuable one reached. Once every programme of a registration has results, the registration is completed and its lane becomes free."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combinations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme marked *combinable with* another programme can take series from it: at registration the shooter picks which series (for example series 2 and 3 of a four-series programme for a two-series programme). The picked series are copied in ascending order and renumbered from 1; the combined programme cannot be edited on its own and follows every change of the source."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:30 ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Awards"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:33
#, markdown-text
msgid "An award tier is available to an age category only if it has a limit for it. A shooter can choose any tier whose limit the total reaches; the most valuable tier is listed first and given by default when the results are saved. The server checks the choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranking {#ranking}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "All results of a programme are ordered by:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "higher total;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "the series compared from the last one backwards (the better last series wins, then the second-to-last, …);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "more mouches;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "age: among juniors (U10–U21) the younger shooter first, among the others the older shooter first; non-juniors rank before juniors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:44
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ranks are consecutive (1, 2, 3, … even on equal results). The same ranking feeds the staff pages, kiosk screens, the ranking PDF and CSV, and special prizes. It was checked against the published rankings of the 2026 Appenzell air pistol championship: identical on all 260 lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:45
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Club competition {#club-competition}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:48
#, markdown-text
msgid "Only programmes marked *counts for the club competition* take part, and only completed results of shooters with a club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "The score of a result is the sum of its first two series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "A club with fewer than 5 participants is listed as *not ranked*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Of *n* participants the best *max(5, ⌊n/2⌋)* are mandatory, the rest are optional."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Result = ⌊(Σ mandatory + 0.02 × Σ optional) / number of mandatory × 1000⌋ / 1000, i.e. truncated to three decimals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ties: more participants first, then the sorted scores compared one by one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:55
#, markdown-text
msgid "The club excluded in the event settings (usually the host) keeps its place in the list but gets no rank (\"out of competition\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:56
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:34
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Special prizes {#special-prizes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:59
#, markdown-text
msgid "A programme can award special prizes to the best ranks of every age category. Three numbers define them:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Ranks per category**, e.g. 3;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "**minimum participants per category** in this programme, e.g. 10;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:63
#, markdown-text
msgid "**minimum participants of the shooter's club** in the same programme, e.g. 4."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:65
#, markdown-text
msgid "Per age category with enough participants, the first shooters in ranking order whose club has enough participants win; shooters whose club has too few are skipped and the next one moves up. Shooters without a club are not eligible unless the club minimum is 0. The report lists both the winners and the skipped shooters with the reason."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:68
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "!!! example \"Appenzell air pistol championship\"\n    The brochure says: *\"In every category, ranks 1–3 receive a special prize, provided the category has at least 10 participants and the shooter's club at least 4.\"* That is ranks 3, category minimum 10, club minimum 4. Applied to the 2026 results, the rule reproduces the hand-made winner list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:69
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lane lists"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:72
#, markdown-text
msgid "Lanes are written as a list of numbers and ranges: `1, 5, 7-10`. Standblatt prints them compactly, turning runs of three or more into ranges (`1-3, 5, 7, 8`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:73
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Money and numbers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/reference/rules.md:75
#, markdown-text
msgid "Amounts are shown as `CHF 1'234.50`, dates as `dd.mm.yyyy`. On wreath cards the value can be printed in words in the event's language, e.g. *Fünfundzwanzig Franken*, *Septante et un francs*, *Ventitré franchi*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "The dashboard is the desk view of an event: who is shooting on which lane, who is waiting, who is done."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Dashboard](../images/screenshots/dashboard.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Shooting**: registrations on a lane, with the time since they started, the buttons **Results**, **Edit** and **Finish**. When the event setting *The organizer hands out the ammunition* is on, **Ammo** records that it was handed out and a green *ammo* badge shows it afterwards (see [Helpers](helpers.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Waiting**: registrations without a lane (for example when all lanes are taken)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Completed**: registrations whose programmes all have results, with an *awards to hand out* badge that opens the results dialog for the handout, or *awards handed out* afterwards (see [Results](results.md#handout))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes**: every lane is *free*, *occupied* (with the shooter), *reserved* (with the reservation and its end) or *out of service*. A reservation shows from its lead time on. An event on several ranges shows one grid per range, and the registration dialog groups the lanes by range; a shooter who moves to another range is finished and registered again there."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "The figures at the top count waiting, shooting and completed registrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "*Waiting* and *Completed* show 50 registrations per page; the arrows below the list turn the pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything updates live: a result entered at another computer or a reservation that starts appears without reloading. The dot next to **live** in the header shows the connection; after a network interruption the page catches up by itself. Without a connection a red bar says so; nothing can be saved then, but open dialogs keep what you typed, so you can save again once you are back online."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:16
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Search and scan"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Press ++f4++ anywhere on the dashboard to jump into the search field."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Search](../images/screenshots/search.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Type a **license number** (digits only, leading zeros optional), a **name** (part of first or last name) or **first and last name** in either order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Each hit offers **Register for &lt;club&gt;** for every club of the shooter, or **Open registration** if the shooter is currently registered."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New shooter** creates a shooter and opens the registration right away."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "A hand scanner reading the [registration code](../reference/codes.md) on a lane sheet or control strip types the code and Enter: the results of that registration open directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Finish shooting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Finish** ends a registration before all results are in, for example when a shooter gives up or hands in the targets later. The registration moves to *Completed* and its lane becomes free; missing results can still be entered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:31
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Dark mode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:34
#, markdown-text
msgid "The sun/moon button in the header switches between light and dark mode; the choice is kept in the browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/dashboard.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Dashboard in dark mode](../images/screenshots/dashboard-dark.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Events** lists the events of the club in the groups *Today* (between the first and the last shooting day), *Upcoming*, *Past* and *Closed*; admins create new ones there. Opening an event shows its dashboard, reservations, rankings, statistics and setup in the sidebar; *Change event* at the top of the sidebar returns to the list.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Events](../images/screenshots/events.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Settings {#settings}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "The event's **Setup** has five tabs: *Programmes* (see [Programmes](programmes.md)), *Event*, *Kiosk displays* (see [Rankings and kiosk](rankings-kiosk.md)), *Helpers* (see [Helpers](helpers.md)) and *Copy & close*. Staff only see the programmes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "The *Event* tab holds the settings (admins):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Setting | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Name, Date, Ranges | the date is the main day; its year sets the age categories (SSV: competition year minus year of birth, the day itself does not matter, which counts for pre-shooting days in December before a January event); tick every range the event is shot on |\n| Shooting days | single days with optional shooting times, for pre-shooting days and multi-day events (registrations count on the day they are made); the main day is always one |\n| Period (season) | for events over weeks or months, e.g. the Feldschiessen from the opening of the range until 31 August: first and last day, plus the weekdays with their shooting times; no weekday ticked means every day. Single days, e.g. the official weekend, add to the period or replace its times on that date |\n| Organizer | printed on documents |\n| Language of documents and kiosk | language of PDFs, CSV exports and kiosk screens, independent of each user's interface language |\n| Club excluded from the club competition | usually the host club; listed as *out of competition* |\n| Show lane status on the rankings | kiosk screens show the lanes |\n| Print the award value on wreath cards | value in figures and words on the card |\n| The organizer hands out the ammunition | shows the **Ammo** button on the dashboard and for the ammunition desk (see [Helpers](helpers.md)); off for events where shooters bring their own, e.g. air pistol and air rifle |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Shooting times also give the online booking its slots, unless the booking sets other hours for a day (see [Online booking](online-booking.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Copy for next year"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:30
#, markdown-text
msgid "On the *Copy & close* tab, **Copy for next year** creates a new event with the same ranges, organizer, language, settings and all programmes, including prices, awards, combinations and special prizes; the shooting days and the period move with the date, weekly shooting times stay on their weekdays. Registrations, results and kiosk links are not copied. The dialog suggests the name with the year (and a leading number like *42.*) counted up and the date one year later; adjust both as needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Copy an event](../images/screenshots/copy-event.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Close {#close}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "When an event is over and the rankings are checked, **Close** it on the *Copy & close* tab. Closing releases the rankings: shooters with a [personal training log](../my-training/account.md#competitions) now find their results of this event, with their rank in the programme, and can add them to their log. Everything stays visible (dashboard, results, rankings, reports, documents), but registrations, results, awards, programmes and settings can no longer be changed. A banner on every page of the event says so. **Reopen** makes it editable again; results that shooters already added to their logs stay there. Copying a closed event for next year works."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Delete"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/events.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Delete** (on the *Copy & close* tab) removes an event, but only while nobody is registered for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Login and language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Logging in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "Log in with the user name (or email address) and password you received from your club admin or the platform operator. Club accounts are not created by sign-up; only [My training](../my-training/account.md) has its own sign-up. Forgot your password? If your account has a confirmed email address, use **Forgot your password?** on the login page; otherwise ask the operator to set a new password in the [admin panel](../admin-guide/admin-panel.md). Logged in, you change it yourself under [Account](#account)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "After the login you land on the start page with a card for every club you belong to and one for [My training](../my-training/index.md), which every user has; **Account** and **Log out** are below the cards. Without a club membership the start page takes you straight to My training."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Start page](../images/screenshots/home.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "A login stays valid for seven days of inactivity and at most 30 days; with **Stay logged in for 90 days** ticked, it lasts 90 days on that device. After too many failed attempts, logins from the same address are blocked for a while."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "If your account belongs to several clubs, you choose the club after logging in; **Switch club** in the user menu goes back to that choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Account {#account}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:20
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Account** in the user menu (bottom of the sidebar), on the start page and in My training's sidebar opens your account settings:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Login**: your user name (it cannot be changed) and your email address. **Add** or **Change** asks for your password and sends a confirmation link; until you confirm, the address counts as *not confirmed* and **Send again** sends a new link. A confirmed address lets you reset a forgotten password yourself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Password**: enter the current and the new password (at least 10 characters). Other devices are logged out, the one you are on stays."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Language and theme**: the interface language of your account and light or dark mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Second factor**: see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Delete account**: only for accounts that belong to no club; the training log, goals and settings are deleted for good. Club accounts are removed by the club admin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:28
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Account](../images/screenshots/account.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Second factor {#totp}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "An authenticator app (Google Authenticator, Aegis, 1Password and the like) can protect your login: after the password, Standblatt asks for the six-digit code the app shows. Set it up under [Account](#account): **Set up**, scan the QR code, enter the current code, **Switch on**. **Switch off** asks for your password. Lost the phone? The operator can reset the second factor in the [admin panel](../admin-guide/admin-panel.md). The operator can also switch the feature off for the whole server."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:36
#, markdown-text
msgid "The interface is available in English, German, French and Italian. Without a choice, Standblatt follows the browser's language. **Language** in the user menu (bottom of the sidebar) sets it for your account on every device."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:38
#, markdown-text
msgid "Printed documents, CSV exports and kiosk screens do not follow your choice but the language of the event, so that every printout of an event looks the same (see [Events](events.md#settings))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:39
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/login-language.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "The bottom of the sidebar shows the version of the server, which helps when reporting a problem; in My training on a phone it is under **Settings**. When a new version is released, open pages offer **Reload** within a minute and load it on the next page change at the latest."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:1
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:26
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Printing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Standblatt renders all documents as PDF:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:12
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Document | Format | When |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lane sheet | A5 | at registration, with QR code and programme barcodes |\n| Control strip | label 90 × 29 mm | at registration, stuck on the target card |\n| Result sheet | A5 | when all programmes have results |\n| Wreath card | A6, printed onto pre-printed cards | after choosing a wreath card award |\n| Ranking | A4 | from the rankings page, as PDF only (not sent to the range's printer) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:14
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every Print button prints on the range's printer if one is set up and its print agent is online; otherwise the PDF opens in the browser and can be printed from there. On a phone or tablet the PDF goes to the share sheet instead (print, save to files, send), so the app stays open; if the phone asks for another tap first, a note with a **Share** button appears."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:15
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setting up printers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:18
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ranges → Printing** (admins):\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:20
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Printing](../images/screenshots/printing.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add print agent**, give it a name and copy the token. Install the agent on a computer next to the printers (see [Print agent](../admin-guide/print-agent.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once the agent is online, it reports its printers. Choose the printer for each document and its options (tray, paper size, media type, further `lp` options such as `fit-to-page`)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Recent jobs** shows what was printed and whether it worked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/printing.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "A job that the agent does not confirm within two minutes is retried; after three attempts it fails. **revoke** removes an agent immediately."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:1
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Programmes belong to an event and are managed on the *Programmes* tab of its **Setup** (admins only)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Setup with the programme list](../images/screenshots/setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Adding programmes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**New programme** opens the editor."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Programme library**: a template of the global library, maintained by the platform operator."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Earlier event**: copies all programmes of another event of the club, including combinations and special prizes. Programmes whose name and variant already exist are skipped."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Add from … → Programme file**: imports a [programme file](../reference/programme-file.md) exported from another event or club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The editor"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Programme editor](../images/screenshots/programme-editor.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Name** and **Variant**: programmes with the same name are variants of each other; a shooter registers for one of them. The name field suggests the names of the event's programmes, and as soon as the name matches one, the editor says that you are creating a variant and warns when the variant name is empty or already taken."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Barcode**: printed on the lane sheet for electronic scoring (see [Codes](../reference/codes.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Counts for the club competition** and **Show on kiosk displays**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Series**: shots, maximum points and whether mouches are tracked, per series."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Prices (CHF)**: only the ticked age categories may shoot the programme."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Awards**: name, kind (wreath card, prize in kind or cash prize paid out in money), value and the minimum total per age category; leave a category empty where the award is not available."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:26
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once shooters are registered for a programme, the **series** are fixed so results keep their meaning; the editor says so and greys them out. Everything else can still be changed: name, variant, description, barcode, the flags, prices, series names, award names, values and limits. Age categories and awards can be **added** but not removed. Also available on a programme in use:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Active**: inactive programmes cannot be chosen for new registrations; existing ones keep them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Combinable with**: the programme whose series this one may take at registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Range** (events on several ranges or ranges with lane groups): the range or lane group the programme is shot on, e.g. *Pistol · 50 m*; the registration then offers only those lanes and kiosk displays group the rankings by range. *any* leaves it open. Programmes of different groups need separate registrations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Special prizes** (see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:33
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Export** downloads the programme as a file; **Delete** is only possible while nobody is registered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:37
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Special prizes** in the programme menu awards the best ranks of every age category, for example ranks 1–3 in every category with at least 10 participants, counting only shooters whose club has at least 4 participants in this programme. Skipped shooters make room for the next one. The exact rule is in [Competition rules](../reference/rules.md#special-prizes); the winners are in the report *Special prizes* under [Statistics](statistics-reports.md).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:39
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Special prizes dialog](../images/screenshots/special-prizes.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/programmes.md:40
#, markdown-text
msgid "Ranks 0 turns special prizes off. The settings can be changed at any time, also after the event."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ranges"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ranges** (admins) lists the shooting ranges of the club.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Ranges](../images/screenshots/ranges.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Name** and **Number of lanes**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Out of service**: lane numbers that cannot be used, e.g. `3, 7`. They show grey on the dashboard and cannot be assigned."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lane groups** (optional): parts of the range with another distance, e.g. a pistol range with `1-10` as *25 m* and `11-15` as *50 m*. The range stays one range with one print agent and shared reservations; the dashboard and kiosk show the groups as headings, and a programme tied to a group only offers its lanes at registration (see [Programmes](programmes.md)). A group used by programmes cannot be removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Printing** opens the printers and print agents of the range (see [Printing](printing.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/ranges.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "A range with events cannot be deleted. Lane reservations belong to the range and show in all of its events (see [Reservations](reservations.md))."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rankings and kiosk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:3
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Rankings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:6
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Rankings** shows a live ranking per programme, ordered by the [SSV rules](../reference/rules.md#ranking). The first three ranks are highlighted.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Rankings](../images/screenshots/rankings.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "**PDF** opens the ranking (A4) for printing or sharing, **CSV** downloads it for Excel. Rankings do not go to the range's printer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:11
#, markdown-text
msgid "Programmes switched off for kiosk displays are still ranked here and marked *not on kiosk*."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:12
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Kiosk screens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "A kiosk link shows the rankings of one event on a screen in the hall, without login. Create one on the *Kiosk displays* tab of the event's **Setup**:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name for the screen (e.g. *Hall 1*), choose **Dark** or **Light** and optionally a language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Create kiosk link**; copy the link. It is shown only once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the link in a browser on the screen, ideally in full screen."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Kiosk screen](../images/screenshots/kiosk.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The kiosk shows only programmes with *Show on kiosk displays* switched on, and the lane status if the event setting *Show lane status on the rankings* is on."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The language is the event's language unless the link carries another one (`?language=de`, `fr`, `it`, `en`); the theme comes from `?theme=dark` or `?theme=light`. On an event with several ranges, `?range=<id>` (chosen when creating the link) limits the display to that range: its lanes, its programmes and the programmes without a range."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The screen updates live and reconnects by itself after a network interruption. When a new version of Standblatt is released, it reloads by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/rankings-kiosk.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "**revoke** in the list stops a link immediately. *last seen* tells when a screen last fetched data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Helpers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Helpers at the event (scorers, the ammunition desk, the results office) work with a **helper link** instead of a login. A helper link opens a reduced desk of one event on any phone or laptop; admins create the links on the *Helpers* tab of the event's **Setup** and revoke them when the event is over."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Scorer's helper page on a phone](../images/screenshots/helper-scorer.png){ .screenshot .phone }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Roles {#roles}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:14
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "| Role | Sees | Can |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Scorer** | the lane grid of their own lanes, the shooters on them | enter results and awards, **Finish** a shooter |\n| **Ammunition desk** | the search box, the waiting list, the shooters on all lanes | mark the ammunition as issued (**Ammo**), assign a lane to a waiting shooter, print the lane sheet |\n| **Results clerk** | the search box, the shooters on all lanes, the completed list | enter results and awards on every lane |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:16
#, markdown-text
msgid "Everything else stays with the club's users: registering shooters, editing programmes, rankings, statistics, deleting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:17
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Creating a link {#create}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "Enter a name (who gets the link, e.g. *Scorer range A*), choose the role and, for a scorer, the range and the lanes (`1-5, 8`). One scorer usually looks after several lanes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Create helper link**; copy the link and send it to the helper (e.g. by messenger). It is shown only once."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:22
#, markdown-text
msgid "The helper opens the link; it stays valid until it is revoked or the event is deleted. `?language=de` (`fr`, `it`, `en`) overrides the event's language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:24
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**revoke** in the list stops a link immediately; *last seen* tells when it was last used. A scorer who opens a shooter on another lane gets *This lane is not yours*.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:25
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Ammunition {#ammunition}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/helpers.md:27
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Ammo** on a waiting or shooting registration records the time the ammunition was handed out; the button exists only when the event setting *The organizer hands out the ammunition* is on (air pistol and air rifle shooters usually bring their own). The dashboard shows a green *ammo* badge on such registrations, so the desk and the range officer see at a glance who has been served.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Registrations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "A registration puts a shooter on a lane with the programmes they shoot. Open it from the dashboard search (**Register for …**)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Registration dialog](../images/screenshots/registration.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lane"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "Pick a free lane in the grid, or leave it empty: the shooter then waits until you assign a lane by editing the registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Occupied and out-of-service lanes cannot be picked."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "A reserved lane asks for confirmation before it is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "The programmes of the event with their price for the shooter's age category. Programmes without a price for that category are greyed out (*not for this age category*)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Variants** (same programme name) appear as a choice of one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "A **combinable** programme offers *take N series from …*: tick it and pick exactly N series of the other programme. The other programme is added automatically if it is not chosen yet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "The **total** at the bottom adds up the prices."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shooter already registered"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "If the shooter is or was registered at this event before, a notice lists those registrations with their programmes and a link to open them. Programmes already booked are locked (*already registered*); a shooter may still shoot another variant in a separate registration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:29
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "*Print lane sheet* and *Print control strip* are ticked by default: the documents print on the range's printers right after registering, or open as PDF if no printer is set up (see [Printing](printing.md)).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:30
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Editing and deleting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/registrations.md:32
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open a registration from the dashboard (**Edit**) or from the results (*Edit registration*) to change the lane or the programmes. Programmes that already have results cannot be removed; changing the picked series of a combination copies the new series. **Delete** removes the registration with its results after a confirmation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Reservations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:4
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Reservations** blocks lanes of the event's range for a time, for example for a training or a group.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Reservations](../images/screenshots/reservations.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes**: a list like `5` or `1, 5, 7-10`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "**From** and **To**: the time span. Reservations on the same lane may not overlap; back-to-back is fine."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Show as reserved (minutes before)**: lead time from which the lanes show as reserved on the dashboard and kiosk."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Reservations belong to the range, so they appear in every event on that range. Reserved lanes can still be assigned to a shooter after a confirmation. The server announces the start and end of reservations by itself, so screens change without reloading."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/reservations.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Requests that external clubs send through [online booking](online-booking.md) are listed above the reservations; once confirmed, they become ordinary reservations named after the club."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:1
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Online booking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "With **online booking**, external clubs ask for lanes themselves. The organizer puts a link into the invitation; a club picks the time slots it wants, says how many lanes it needs in each and announces its shooters. An admin confirms or declines every request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:5
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Switching it on {#setup}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:8
#, markdown-text
msgid "On the *Online booking* tab of the event's **Setup**, **Switch on** is all it takes. The tab then shows the link with a QR code for the invitation and the slots it offers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:10
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Online booking in the setup](../images/screenshots/booking-setup.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:12
#, markdown-text
msgid "Without changes, every day of the event is open during its shooting times (see [Events](events.md#settings)), or from 08:00 to 17:00 when it has none, in slots of 30 minutes, and requests are accepted until 14 days before the first day. **Adjust** changes this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Shooting from** and **Shooting until**: the hours of every day without shooting times."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Break from** and **Break until**: an optional break, e.g. for lunch."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Slot length (minutes)**: how long one slot is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Lanes per slot and club**: a limit per request; empty means no limit."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Deadline**: the last day clubs can ask or change their request."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:19
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Days with other hours**: one line per day of the event, e.g. Friday 17:00–20:00. The days come from the event and follow it when you add or remove one."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:21
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**New link** replaces the link; the old one stops working. **Switch off** closes the booking; requests and confirmed reservations stay. *Copy for next year* takes the hours along, but not the link and not the deadline.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "What a club sees {#club}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:25
#, markdown-text
msgid "The link opens a page without login. It shows the event, the deadline and every slot with the lanes still free on each range. Only confirmed reservations count; names of other clubs are never shown."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:27
#, markdown-text
msgid "![The booking page of a club](../images/screenshots/booking-public.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:29
#, markdown-text
msgid "The club enters the number of lanes per slot, its name, a contact person, email and phone, and its **Shooters**: last name, first name, birthday and optionally the licence. **Paste list** takes rows copied from Excel (last name, first name, birthday, licence). The shooter list can follow later; programmes are chosen at the range as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:31
#, markdown-text
msgid "After **Send request**, the club gets a mail with a personal link. Through it, it can check the status, change the request or cancel it until the deadline. Changing the slots of a confirmed request releases its lanes and the request waits for a new confirmation; adding shooters keeps it confirmed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:32
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Confirming requests {#confirm}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:35
#, markdown-text
msgid "Every admin with an email gets a mail for each new, changed or cancelled request. The requests are listed at the top of **Reservations**; the sidebar shows how many are waiting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:37
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Booking requests on the reservations page](../images/screenshots/booking-requests.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** gives each slot free lanes of its range, neighbours where possible, as an ordinary reservation named after the club, and mails the lane numbers to the club. When a slot has too few free lanes, nothing is reserved and the message names the slot; move a reservation or decline."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Confirm** also takes the shooters into the master data: a shooter is found by licence, else by name and birthday, and created otherwise; the club is created when needed. Existing shooters are never overwritten, because the list comes from a public form; only a missing birthday or licence is filled in. Shooters added after the confirmation are taken over with **Take over shooters**."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:41
#, markdown-text
msgid "**Decline** asks for an optional reason, which goes to the club by mail. Lanes the request held are free again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/online-booking.md:42
#, markdown-text
msgid "The reserved lanes are ordinary [reservations](reservations.md): change their lane numbers there if needed. At the event, the shooters are found with the normal search at the registration desk. The report *Lane bookings* under [Statistics and reports](statistics-reports.md) lists every club with its slots, lanes and shooters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:4
#, markdown-text
msgid "Open the results of a registration with the **Results** button on the dashboard or by scanning the code on the lane sheet."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:6
#, markdown-text
msgid "![Results dialog](../images/screenshots/results.png){ .screenshot }"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:7
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Entering series"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "The cursor starts in the first empty series. As soon as another digit would exceed the series maximum, it moves on to the next field, so a sequence like `96 93 97 88` can be typed without the mouse."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Series that track mouches have a second field for them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "++enter++ or **Save** stores the programme. Values above the maximum are marked and cannot be saved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:13
#, markdown-text
msgid "Saving again replaces the results; the chosen award stays as long as the new total still reaches it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:15
#, markdown-text
msgid "A combined programme shows which series it takes from its source programme and fills in automatically once the source has results."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:17
#, markdown-text
msgid "When every programme has results, the registration is completed and its lane is free again. **Print result sheet** prints an A5 summary for the shooter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:21
#, markdown-text
msgid "Once a programme is complete, the awards the total reaches in the shooter's age category are listed, the most valuable first; of several wreath cards (or several prizes in kind) only the most valuable one reached is offered. Saving the results already gives the most valuable one; picking another one saves it at once. For a wreath card, **Print wreath card** prints the shooter's data onto a pre-printed A6 card; the value is printed only if the event setting *Print the award value on wreath cards* is on (in figures and in words)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:22
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Handing out awards {#handout}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../src/help/en/user-guide/results.md:24
#, markdown-text
msgid "When the shooter collects the wreath cards, prizes and cash at the desk, press **Awards handed out** in the results dialog, which lists the awards of every programme; the *awards to hand out* badge in the *Completed* list of the dashboard opens that dialog. The registration then carries the time of the handout and a green *awards handed out* badge; until then it shows *awards to hand out*. A wrong click is taken back with **Take back** in the results dialog or by clicking the green badge on the dashboard (club members only, not helper links); the same works for the *ammo* badge. The report **Awards to hand out** (see [Statistics and reports](statistics-reports.md)) lists what is still open and the cash to pay out. A results clerk with a [helper link](helpers.md) may mark awards as handed out too."
msgstr ""

